184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (I visited Magnus Wharf at Gangolli Port expecting a range of boatyard sites I could compare against each other.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
185 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (What I found instead was one main shelter area, used by everything from large ferries down to small fishing boats, simply because it has been the shelter area for years.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 152 0 R
/E (There was not enough variety of sites to build a comparison from, so the whole basis of my original project did not hold up once I tested it against the real place. I also learned there is no fixed manual for building boats. The process is understood through experience and instinct, passed on rather than written down.)
