/S /P
/P 156 0 R
/E (The paper argues that the plan shows new urban infrastructure along the water's edge around Kundapura town, threatening intertidal ecologies and the livelihoods of communities who depend on the estuary and its wetlands.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
243 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 156 0 R
/E (It points out that the Master Plan drawing works with only four land use categories, Developed Area, Agricultural Area, Marshy Area, and Water Sheet, leaving no room for the riparian ecotones between land and water that regulate salinity, absorb flooding, and support the flora and fauna of the estuary. This gave my own observations a proper, sourced reason to be tested rather than left as a hunch.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
